IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cra-cremation`
IMPORT `cra-qa`

-- Cremation Act 1929 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (cra-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every
-- situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for the three roles it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none:
-- the answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation with an error
-- ("it is an assumed term"). Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with FALSE and
-- every later input ASSUMEd: again `does not arise for you`. For the arranger (the baseline's seat) each answer is also
-- asserted equal to the baseline export's own answer on the same facts. Expected values are worked by hand from the
-- deposited text, never copied from the output.
--
-- Facts: Graham's death (c086) and Chloe's (c098), with the baseline's fixtures (cra-cases-cremation.l4), restated
-- here. As there, that each death was natural and certified by the deceased's own GP, and the funeral director's
-- authority, are ASSUMED.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked applicant` IS AN Applicant
ASSUME `an unasked death` IS A Death
ASSUME `an unasked doctor` IS A Doctor
ASSUME `an unasked day` IS A `Day the permit is given`

`as the arranger` MEANS `I am arranging the cremation of someone who has died`
`as the family` MEANS `I am the spouse, de facto partner or next of kin of someone who has died`
`as the crematorium` MEANS `I run a licensed crematorium`
`as the doctor` MEANS `I am the doctor certifying the cause of death`

`Chloe, Graham's executor` MEANS Applicant WITH
    `is the executor named in the will` IS TRUE
    `has the best right to apply for administration` IS FALSE
    `has lawful custody of the body` IS FALSE
    `acts with the written authority of and on behalf of the administrator` IS FALSE
    `the referee is satisfied the administrator will not apply, of my reason, and that I am a proper person` IS FALSE
    `knows that a spouse, de facto partner or next of kin has objected in writing` IS FALSE

`Chloe, Graham's executor, knowing Sue has objected in writing` MEANS Applicant WITH
    `is the executor named in the will` IS TRUE
    `has the best right to apply for administration` IS FALSE
    `has lawful custody of the body` IS FALSE
    `acts with the written authority of and on behalf of the administrator` IS FALSE
    `the referee is satisfied the administrator will not apply, of my reason, and that I am a proper person` IS FALSE
    `knows that a spouse, de facto partner or next of kin has objected in writing` IS TRUE

`the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` MEANS Applicant WITH
    `is the executor named in the will` IS FALSE
    `has the best right to apply for administration` IS FALSE
    `has lawful custody of the body` IS FALSE
    `acts with the written authority of and on behalf of the administrator` IS TRUE
    `the referee is satisfied the administrator will not apply, of my reason, and that I am a proper person` IS FALSE
    `knows that a spouse, de facto partner or next of kin has objected in writing` IS FALSE

`the funeral director, holding Graham's body` MEANS Applicant WITH
