-- Mirror cases. c086: Sue objects in writing and Graham's will says nothing of cremation -- the arranger's question and
-- the family's agree; and the crematorium may not cremate.
#ASSERT `Does a written objection by the family stop the cremation` `as the arranger` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Does my written objection stop the cremation` `as the family` TRUE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I cremate this body now` `as the crematorium` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing` TRUE 48 TRUE EQUALS no
-- ... with Graham's attested will asking for cremation, all three turn.
#ASSERT `Does a written objection by the family stop the cremation` `as the arranger` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing; Graham's attested will asks for cremation` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does my written objection stop the cremation` `as the family` TRUE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I cremate this body now` `as the crematorium` `c086 variant: Sue has objected in writing; Graham's attested will asks for cremation` TRUE 48 TRUE EQUALS yes
-- c098: the ashes go to Oliver, who obtained the permit, and not to Ella -- from each seat.
#ASSERT `May the crematorium deliver the ashes to me` `as the arranger` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May the ashes be given to me as family` `as the family` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I deliver the ashes to this person` `as the crematorium` TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
-- The doctor's certificate, from the arranger's seat and the doctor's.
#ASSERT `Can the doctor's certificate support the cremation permit` `as the arranger` `a doctor married to the deceased, who inherits` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Can my certificate of cause of death support a cremation permit` `as the doctor` `a doctor married to the deceased, who inherits` EQUALS no

§§ `For the family member, executor or funeral director arranging the cremation (the baseline's seat)`

-- Am I an administrator of the deceased?
-- c086: the executor.
#ASSERT `Am I an administrator of the deceased` `as the arranger` `Chloe, Graham's executor` EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Am I an administrator of the deceased` `as the arranger` `Chloe, Graham's executor` EQUALS (`yes if` (`Am I an administrator` `Chloe, Graham's executor`))
-- Authority does not make the funeral director an administrator.
#ASSERT `Am I an administrator of the deceased` `as the arranger` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Am I an administrator of the deceased` `as the arranger` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority` EQUALS (`yes if` (`Am I an administrator` `the funeral director, with Chloe's written authority`))
#ASSERT `Am I an administrator of the deceased` `as the family` `an unasked applicant` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Am I an administrator of the deceased` `as the crematorium` `an unasked applicant` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Am I an administrator of the deceased` `as the doctor` `an unasked applicant` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

